            "review_title": "Review at Hanayuki No.1 Hanoi",
            "review_text": "CGL_17\nSingapore, Singapore97 contributions\n0\nFor really fresh sashimi, etc\nNov 2018 • Business\nThis was the second time I have dined at Hanayuki and the restaurant has not failed to impress me with the freshness of their sashimi platter. The platter had slices of tuna, salmon, yellow tail, scallops and other varieties of shellfish and they were really fresh. What I liked about having the sashimi here is that they also provide you with a plate of seaweed sheets which you use to wrap the slices of raw fish with. Makes it taste quite different from just eating the raw fish on its own. The salmon hotpot dish is another must try, with lots of accompanying vegetables and mushrooms. Last but not least, for starters, try the octopus marinated with sea grapes.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 2, 2018",
